<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf8" />
    <title>{{title}}</title>
    <!-- needed for adaptive design -->
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <style>
      body {
        padding: 0;
        margin: 0;
      }
    </style>
    {{!--
      The renderer's default page (see build.sh) with one addition: the sidebar logo carries the
      page's name beneath it. Redoc has no option for a logo caption, and the logo image is the
      wordmark alone, so the caption is drawn by CSS on the logo link the renderer emits - the
      link's target is the `x-logo.href` of src/index.yaml, which is what the selector keys on.
      The logo's size and spacing come from `theme.logo` in redocly.yaml.
    --}}
    <style>
      .menu-content a[href="https://www.humhub.com"] {
        display: block;
        text-align: center;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
      /* The renderer sizes the image as a block, so it centres by margin, not by text-align. */
      .menu-content a[href="https://www.humhub.com"] img {
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      }
      .menu-content a[href="https://www.humhub.com"]::after {
        content: "API Reference";
        display: block;
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #6f7a80;
      }
    </style>
    {{{redocHead}}}
    {{#unless disableGoogleFont}}<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Montserrat:300,400,700|Roboto:300,400,700" rel="stylesheet">{{/unless}}
  </head>
  <body>
    {{{redocHTML}}}
  </body>
</html>
